WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:02.602
-Our first guest tonight is
a Grammy-nominated comedian

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:04.003
and best-selling author.

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:06.572
She is currently out on her
"Vaccinated and Horny" tour.

00:00:06.572 --> 00:00:07.673
Please welcome back to the show

00:00:07.673 --> 00:00:10.043
our friend Chelsea handler,
everybody!

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:12.044
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.044 --> 00:00:17.650 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:23.189 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:25.724
You look stunning, as always.
It's so wonderful to see you.

00:00:25.724 --> 00:00:26.993
-Oh, it's wonderful to see you.

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:29.195
I had no idea Fred Armisen
was working here now.

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:31.063
-Isn't that wonderful?
-Yeah, hello, Fred.

00:00:31.063 --> 00:00:32.232
-Hi, nice to see you.

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:33.933
-It's very nice for
a couple of our guests

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:37.637
to almost bring a collaboration
when they come on the show.

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:38.838
Obviously, you did not know
when you were coming

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:40.072
that Martha Stewart was going to
be on the show,

00:00:40.072 --> 00:00:42.174
but Martha posted this photo of
herself

00:00:42.174 --> 00:00:44.677
a couple years ago in her pool,
a very beautiful photo.

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:47.413
And then how quickly
did you do that?

00:00:47.413 --> 00:00:49.648
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.648 --> 00:00:52.085
-Well, I mean, I've always
looked up to Martha.

00:00:52.085 --> 00:00:54.320
-Who doesn't? Yeah.
-For obvious reasons.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:57.122
And it wasn't long after
I saw that shot.

00:00:57.122 --> 00:00:59.426
I saw myself in her shot,

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:02.061
and I realized that I could
reproduce that pretty quickly.

00:01:02.061 --> 00:01:03.262
-And what was her feedback?

00:01:03.262 --> 00:01:04.797
Because she had some feedback
for you.

00:01:04.797 --> 00:01:07.867
-Her feedback was that her pool
was a lot nicer than my pool.

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:09.769
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:12.572
-I mean, she's not lying, right?
-Well, I don't know that.

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:14.307
I mean, can we compare pools?

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:15.941
Did we get a full view
of either pool?

00:01:15.941 --> 00:01:17.810
-I don't know.
Her pool looks super nice.

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:19.345
-Okay, well, it sounds like --

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:22.115
It sounds like you have a
favorite out of the two of us.

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:24.750
-I'm just saying, if you both
invited me to a pool party,

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:26.385
I'm, like, at Martha's house
in five minutes.

00:01:26.385 --> 00:01:27.954
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:30.790
Got it. Got it. Okay.
Good to know.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:33.959
-So you're touring your show,
"Vaccinated and Horny."

00:01:33.959 --> 00:01:35.528
Feels like it's
self-explanatory,

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:37.296
but is there more to it?

00:01:37.296 --> 00:01:38.698
-Well, I guess --

00:01:38.698 --> 00:01:41.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:43.870
I guess, you know,
it's very representative of

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:45.672
being single
during the pandemic.

00:01:45.672 --> 00:01:47.440
-Right.
-Married people were dealing

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:50.276
with their own, you know,
set of issues,

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:51.978
like being married.
-Yeah.

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:54.647
-Or having children.
-Yeah.

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:56.515
-Or having to homeschool
those children.

00:01:56.515 --> 00:01:59.685
Single people were just -- I was
at home having a great time,

00:01:59.685 --> 00:02:01.653
well, with my landscaper,
mostly,

00:02:01.653 --> 00:02:04.858
because it was just the two of
us for a couple of weeks.

00:02:04.858 --> 00:02:06.592
[ Laughter ]
And at a certain point,

00:02:06.592 --> 00:02:09.329
it's not fun to do mushrooms
alone, so I moved him in.

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:10.796
-That's great.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.796 --> 00:02:13.332
-And vaccinated and horny is
just how I thought the whole --

00:02:13.332 --> 00:02:15.701
you know,
how all single people felt

00:02:15.701 --> 00:02:17.570
as soon as we were allowed out.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:20.472
And it was a dangerous time
because if all single people

00:02:20.472 --> 00:02:23.309
get out at the same time
and start penetrating...

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:25.711
-Yeah.
-Then, you know, there's gonna

00:02:25.711 --> 00:02:29.215
be, like, a new STD strain
or something like cov-erpes

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:31.083
or something along those lines.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.083 --> 00:02:34.787
So I wanted to avoid that
but make sure everybody knew

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:36.089
that I was the place to come

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:37.957
if you were single, vaccinated,
and horny.

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:39.892
-That's really nice
because I'm sure, like,

00:02:39.892 --> 00:02:42.061
those people, for the purposes
of buying the ticket,

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:43.396
they also get a night of
entertainment,

00:02:43.396 --> 00:02:44.564
but also you've let them know

00:02:44.564 --> 00:02:46.098
some important information
about yourself.

00:02:46.098 --> 00:02:48.167
-Yes, yes, and this was before

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:52.138
I started my love affair
with my boyfriend, Mr. Jo Koy.

00:02:52.138 --> 00:02:54.073
So I still am
vaccinated and horny,

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:55.741
but it's now directed
at one person.

00:02:55.741 --> 00:02:57.376
-That's great.
So this is interesting,

00:02:57.376 --> 00:02:58.511
'cause you're single
during the pandemic.

00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:00.779
And obviously,
your boyfriend Jo,

00:03:00.779 --> 00:03:02.148
who's also a super-talented
comedian,

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:03.148
but you've known him forever.

00:03:03.148 --> 00:03:04.617
You guys met on
"Chelsea Lately."

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:07.520
-Uh-huh.
-Do you now, because --

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:09.222
Basically, you did know him
during the pandemic.

00:03:09.222 --> 00:03:11.090
Do you look back and are you mad
that you didn't meet him

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:12.258
in the beginning,
just so you guys

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:14.360
would go through it together?

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:16.095
-No, I'm pretty glad that I went

00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:17.963
through that pandemic
mostly solo.

00:03:17.963 --> 00:03:19.498
-Okay.
-I mean, my sister did come

00:03:19.498 --> 00:03:21.601
and invade my house
with her three children,

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:23.635
which is something I've worked
pretty hard

00:03:23.635 --> 00:03:25.471
to avoid my whole life.
-Yeah.

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:27.540
-So that was a slight hiccup.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:30.809
But I think the pandemic was
better, if you could do it solo,

00:03:30.809 --> 00:03:33.413
I think it was a good thing
to do solo.

00:03:33.413 --> 00:03:35.682
-I've heard you. I believe you
and I have even talked about

00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:36.882
your sister
and her three children,

00:03:36.882 --> 00:03:39.552
and you have often framed it
as an invasion.

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:42.454
And I'm wondering --
-Yeah, it was a home invasion.

00:03:42.454 --> 00:03:44.757
That's what I call it.
I sold that house.

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:46.759
Actually, I put it on the market
while they were still

00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:48.994
living there, to send a message.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.994 --> 00:03:52.097
And I promptly sold that house.

00:03:52.097 --> 00:03:54.666
I moved out of that house,
and I bought a new house

00:03:54.666 --> 00:03:57.336
and I have converted any extra
bedroom into something

00:03:57.336 --> 00:03:59.839
that is not a bedroom.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.839 --> 00:04:03.543
-So not even something like
a home gym that you could turn

00:04:03.543 --> 00:04:05.578
into a bedroom for the weekend?
-No.

00:04:05.578 --> 00:04:07.580
No, I don't have
any extra bedrooms.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:09.515
And my sister is like,
"That seems pretty drastic.

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:10.749
You have a pretty big family."

00:04:10.749 --> 00:04:12.784
And I'm like, "Well, these are
the new rules."

00:04:12.784 --> 00:04:15.855
You know, we vacation together
a couple times a year.

00:04:15.855 --> 00:04:17.724
I think that's plenty.
-Yeah.

00:04:17.724 --> 00:04:20.726
How do the kids feel about
their aunt

00:04:20.726 --> 00:04:22.728
referring to them
as home invaders?

00:04:22.728 --> 00:04:23.896
-They're used to me

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:25.331
because they've known me
since they were born.

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:26.833
So they know that
they're just lucky

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:28.601
I'm not saying anything worse,
you know?

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:30.903
But actually, that's not true
because in my stand-up show,

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:33.473
I do talk about my nephew a lot.

00:04:33.473 --> 00:04:35.140
I was a little bit worried
about that

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:37.476
because as a public figure,
when you talk about your family,

00:04:37.476 --> 00:04:39.345
they can be very sensitive
about that.

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:41.280
And it's hard. It's a conflict
because it's like,

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:43.649
it's my story, too.
-Yeah.

00:04:43.649 --> 00:04:45.651
-So I --
-Yeah, that would be like

00:04:45.651 --> 00:04:47.920
Chelsea erasure if you're not
allowed to talk about it.

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:49.422
-Yeah, right.
-How old is he?

00:04:49.422 --> 00:04:52.191
-He's 24.
-Oh, that's okay. Come on.

00:04:52.191 --> 00:04:53.760
-Yeah, right.
-I mean, you're talking about

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:55.194
a nephew, I think a lot of us
are like,

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:57.630
"That poor 7-year-old."
-Yeah.

00:04:57.630 --> 00:05:00.399
-Yeah, just in case,
his name is Jake Hutchinson.

00:05:00.399 --> 00:05:02.902
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.902 --> 00:05:04.770
So if people want to Facebook
him and verify the age.

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:07.006
-Just in case you want to find
out more about him,

00:05:07.006 --> 00:05:08.674
that's his name.

00:05:08.674 --> 00:05:10.108
-I have a lot more questions
for you.

00:05:10.108 --> 00:05:12.211
We'll be right back with more
from Chelsea Handler.

